{
  "name": "Dealing with Persistent Interior Wear and Tear",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Persistent interior wear and tear can be frustrating, especially when it keeps reappearing. The first step is always to inspect the affected area thoroughly. Don't just look at the surface; try to understand what's causing the problem. Are you seeing bubbling paint, recurring stains, or drywall damage? It's crucial to check for moisture, as this is often the culprit for many interior issues. If you find moisture, identifying and fixing the source is absolutely essential before any cosmetic repairs begin. Once the cause is handled, you can move on to making the surface repair. This usually involves prepping the area, applying the necessary patch or filler, then sanding, priming, and finally repainting or refinishing to blend it seamlessly with the surrounding area. Skipping any of these steps can mean the repair won't last. If the damage is widespread, caused by mold or extensive moisture, or involves structural elements of drywall or ceilings, it’s definitely time to bring in a professional. HH Remodeling LLC, serving the Denver area, can help diagnose and fix these interior wear and tear issues properly. Reach out to us at 303-505-0866.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
